From AstraDroneOpen
Subject: [PATCH] Allow opt-in per-goal height in EGO manual waypoint mode

This is the approved minimal vendor patch applied to the bundled EGO planner.
The existing fixed-height behavior remains the default.  Setting
`fsm/use_goal_height=true` makes the manual waypoint callback consume each
incoming goal z after finite/positive validation.  The patch includes a small
unit-tested selector and launch plumbing; it does not alter the planner's
trajectory optimizer or obstacle/map code.

Applied files:
  planner/plan_manage/include/plan_manage/goal_height.h
  planner/plan_manage/include/plan_manage/ego_replan_fsm.h
  planner/plan_manage/src/ego_replan_fsm.cpp
  planner/plan_manage/launch/advanced_param.xml
  planner/plan_manage/CMakeLists.txt
  planner/plan_manage/package.xml
  planner/plan_manage/test/goal_height_test.cpp

The exact source changes are intentionally kept in the working tree above so
the patch can be regenerated against a future vendor baseline with `git diff`.
